---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../components/SiteFooter.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy | kitcheck.cc"
  description="Privacy policy for kitcheck.cc. Learn what data we collect, why, and how it is used."
  canonical="https://kitcheck.cc/privacy/"
>
  <SiteHeader slot="header">
    <a href="/" class="btn-primary">Use the calculator</a>
  </SiteHeader>

  <section class="bg-bg">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="max-w-2xl pt-16 md:pt-18 lg:pt-20 pb-12 md:pb-14">
        <nav class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs text-text-light mb-5">
          <a href="/" class="hover:text-text-mid transition-colors">kitcheck.cc</a>
          <span>›</span>
          <span class="text-text-mid">Privacy policy</span>
        </nav>
        <h1 class="font-head text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight leading-[1.1] text-text mb-4">
          Privacy policy
        </h1>
        <p class="text-text-mid leading-relaxed">
          Last updated: October 2026
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-bg border-t border-border">
    <div class="container py-14 md:py-18">
      <div class="max-w-2xl prose-custom">

        <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
        <p>
          kitcheck.cc is a free, personal project run by Ties Kuiper in the Netherlands.
          He is the controller for the personal data described on this page. Questions or
          requests can be sent to <a href="mailto:privacy@kitcheck.cc">privacy@kitcheck.cc</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>In short</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>No account, no forms, no newsletter: we never ask who you are.</li>
          <li>Google Analytics only runs if you click <em>Accept</em>, and you can change that any time.</li>
          <li>Your exact location never leaves your browser; GPX files are never uploaded.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Hosting (Cloudflare)</h2>
        <p>
          The site is hosted on Cloudflare. Like any web server, Cloudflare processes
          your IP address and basic request data (page, browser, time) to deliver the site and
          protect it against abuse. Cloudflare, Inc. acts as our processor and is certified under
          the EU-US Data Privacy Framework.
          <br />Legal basis: our legitimate interest in running a secure, working website
          (GDPR Article 6(1)(f)).
        </p>


        <h2>Google Analytics (only with your consent)</h2>
        <p>
          If you click <em>Accept</em> in the cookie banner, we load Google Analytics 4 to
          understand how the calculator is used. Before you accept, nothing is sent to Google.
          Google Analytics then records:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Pages you visit, how you arrived (e.g. a search engine) and how long you stay</li>
          <li>Your approximate location (country and city, derived from your IP address; Google Analytics 4 does not store the IP address itself)</li>
          <li>Device type, browser and operating system</li>
          <li>
            How you use the calculator: how you chose a location (search, suggestion,
            auto-detect or GPX), the intensity, warmth, unit, day, start time and duration you
            pick, the average speed you set and the distance of an uploaded route, and the
            conditions of the recommendation you get. We never send location names,
            coordinates or route files.
          </li>
          <li>Errors (for example a failed forecast or an unreadable GPX file) and clicks on the Raas Racing Team links</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Google Analytics recognises a returning browser with a cookie (see the <a href="/cookies/">cookie policy</a>). Google signals and all advertising features are
          switched off; the data is not used for ads. Google Ireland Ltd. processes the data on our
          behalf; data may be transferred to Google LLC in the United States under the EU-US Data
          Privacy Framework.
          <br />Legal basis: your consent (GDPR Article 6(1)(a)). You can withdraw it at any time
          via <em>Cookie settings</em> at the bottom of every page; we then stop Google Analytics
          and delete its cookies. Withdrawing does not affect data collected before.
        </p>

        <h2>Weather and place names</h2>
        <p>
          To show a forecast, your browser sends the place you search for, or rounded coordinates
          (about 1&nbsp;km precise), to <a href="https://open-meteo.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open-Meteo</a>.
          When you use auto-detect or upload a GPX route, rounded coordinates are also sent to <a href="https://nominatim.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Nominatim</a> (OpenStreetMap)
          to find the place name. Auto-detect only works after you allow it in your browser.
          For a GPX route, a set of rounded points along the route (with their altitude) is sent
          to Open-Meteo, so the forecast covers the whole ride rather than just the start.
          Your GPX file itself is read in your browser and never uploaded. We do not store any of this.
          <br />Legal basis: our legitimate interest in providing the calculator you are using
          (GDPR Article 6(1)(f)).
        </p>

        <h2>Maps and fonts</h2>
        <p>
          Route maps load map images from <a href="https://openfreemap.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">OpenFreeMap</a>, or from <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">OpenStreetMap</a> as a
          fallback. These services receive your IP address when your browser requests the
          map, as with any website. Fonts are served from kitcheck.cc itself, not from Google.
        </p>

        <h2>How long data is kept</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Google Analytics: 2 months for individual event data, then deleted automatically; only aggregated reports are kept longer</li>
          <li>Your cookie choice: 12 months in your browser, after which we ask again</li>
          <li>Your average speed for GPX routes (if you set one): in your browser only, until you reset it</li>
          <li>Your choice of °C or °F (if you switch): in your browser only</li>
          <li>Weather and place name lookups: not stored by us</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          You have the right to access, correct or delete your personal data, to restrict or
          object to processing, to data portability, and to withdraw consent at any time. Because
          we cannot link analytics data to you, we may ask for details (such as your Google
          Analytics cookie ID) to find it. Send requests to <a href="mailto:privacy@kitcheck.cc">privacy@kitcheck.cc</a>; we respond within one month.
        </p>
        <p>
          You can also file a complaint with the Dutch data protection authority, the <a href="https://autoriteitpersoonsgegevens.nl" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Autoriteit Persoonsgegevens</a>,
          or the authority in your own EU country.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          If we change how we handle data, we update this page and the date at the top. If the
          change affects cookies, the banner asks for your consent again.
        </p>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <SiteFooter slot="footer" />
</Base>

<style>
  .prose-custom h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-head, inherit);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin-top: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  .prose-custom p,
  .prose-custom ul {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--color-text-mid);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  .prose-custom ul {
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    list-style: disc;
  }
  .prose-custom li {
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }
  .prose-custom a {
    color: var(--color-coral);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .prose-custom a:hover {
    opacity: 0.75;
  }
</style>
